course: dictionary
lesson: 422
title: The month of April
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: April is a month, the fourth month of the year. It has 30 days. Month names are proper nouns, so they always start with a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence.
explain: Context helps you think about the word. «It is spring in April in the northern half of the world, but autumn in Australia and New Zealand.» The words around April show that the season depends on where you live.
explain: Read the phrase «April showers». Showers are short bursts of rain, so April showers means rain that falls now and then during the month of April. Words work together, so look at the whole phrase.
fact: April is the fourth month of the year and has 30 days.
fact: In the northern half of the world, April is spring; in Australia and New Zealand, it is autumn.
fact: «April Fools' Day» is 1 April, when people in many countries play harmless tricks and tell made-up news.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, tradition says April Fool tricks are done before midday; whoever pranks after noon is the fool.
fact: Many news websites publish joke stories on April Fools' Day, so check the date and think before you believe them.
exercise: How many days does April have? | 31 | 28 | 29 | *30
exercise: In the northern half of the world, which season is April? | Summer | *Spring | Winter | Autumn
exercise: In «we walk the dog in april», which word needs a capital letter? | dog | *april | walk | we
test: April is the ___ month of the year. | Second | *Fourth | Fifth | Third
test: On April Fools' Day, what do people often do? | Go to bed early | *Play harmless tricks and tell made-up news | Read the dictionary all day | Plant trees in the snow
exam: In Australia, which season is April? | Summer | Winter | *Autumn | Spring
